[ti:油门焊死]
[ar:Suno V6]
[al:Throttle Welded Shut]
[by:作词 老梁 / Gemini Hydrogen / Opus]
[00:04.30] 2026, Tokyo. Don't brake.
[00:22.13] The rice balls at the convenience store got new price tags again this morning
[00:24.48] The yen sets a new low every day, crashing straight through the floor
[00:26.61] Chairman Gao slams the table: "Found the root cause — too many foreigners!"
[00:30.15] Permanent residency now needs a Japanese exam; nine in ten Business Manager visas vanish
[00:32.40] "Orderly coexistence" in plain speech: please line up neatly… and walk far away
[00:36.30] I say great! Whoever dares stop this acceleration is a traitor
[00:40.30] Prices are flying, the yen is falling
[00:42.70] The news says everything's fine
[00:45.00] Then don't stop, don't touch the brake
[00:47.10] Crank the volume to the max
[00:51.40] Floor the gas, don't look back
[00:53.80] Weld the doors shut, make the wall longer
[00:56.10] How beautiful these golden-age fireworks are
[00:58.90] Everyone on board, sing with me
[01:00.90] Banzai, banzai, a boundless future
[01:03.30] Accelerate all the way, toward glory
[01:05.40] Harder! Faster!
[01:09.60] Hey! AI writes poetry now, and the ward office is still waiting on a fax machine
[01:12.50] Read the air, memorize the rules — you call it etiquette, I call it collective suffocation
[01:16.30] Resident tax, income tax, pension — deducted on time every month, down to the last yen
[01:19.10] Renting starts with "your nationality?"; renewing a visa means reading every face and mood
[01:22.00] They send us to night shifts, construction sites, and nursing care
[01:24.20] while cursing us online for stealing your benefits
[01:26.40] OK, I'll leave
[01:27.50] No hard feelings
[01:28.30] May your rusty machine spin out a miracle soon
[01:32.30] Alarms are blaring, the gauges are jumping
[01:34.50] A wall ahead — I knew it all along
[01:36.80] Then speed up, whatever you do, don't stop
[01:38.80] Push the speed to the limit
[01:43.00] Faster, faster, don't stop
[01:45.50] Throttle welded down, charging ahead
[01:47.60] I can't wait to hear that giant crash
[01:50.20] Everyone on board, sing with me
[01:52.40] Faster! Faster! The faster the better!
[01:54.60] Race wildly onward, charging into glory.
[01:56.90] Don't brake! Don't even think of jumping out!
[02:01.50] Solid-state battery mass production keeps slipping; BYD is already parked outside your door
[02:06.20] Nissan and Honda got engaged and split right away; the home-appliance supergroup is sold off and broken up
[02:10.40] Trillions in chip subsidies, shouting "Rapidus will be back!"
[02:13.00] Population shrinks by a whole city every year; empty houses go to auction for 1 yen
[02:15.40] Population decline? What the hell do I care?
[02:16.50] The future looks grim? Not my problem
[02:17.90] Net-right types shouting "split the social security accounts"? Brother, that's wonderful
[02:19.60] No more supporting your parents — my payslip just grows an extra line
[02:22.10] I've got a passport in my pocket, and flights leave for far away every day
[02:24.20] When everyone who pushes wheelchairs is gone, guard your own parents' sickbeds yourselves
[02:29.70] Don't stop!
[02:31.50] That giant crash — I've waited so long.
[02:35.90] Karma is on the way.
[02:38.40] Don't stop (the faster the better)
[02:41.80] Over the cliff (flying to heaven)
[02:44.10] Till the bill arrives at your own door
[02:47.70] Everyone sing once more — the last time
[02:50.90] Long live Chairman Gao, ten thousand years without end
[02:53.50] Vice-Chairman Xiaoyetian, forever in good health
[03:00.10] Chairman Gao, long life, never stop.
[03:02.40] Chairman Gao, long life, without end.
[03:04.60] Xiaoyetian, long life without end
[03:06.90] Vice-Chairman Xiaoyetian,
[03:10.45] Forever, forever healthy.
[03:18.93] May you run things better and better. Long life without end.
[03:24.64] Long life without end
[03:28.83] Forever healthy.
